---
code: K0009
title: Function Without Parenthesis
severity: ERROR
since: 0.1.0
category: parse
deprecated: False
tags: [ parse, syntax, function, declaration ]
description: "Function declaration is missing a parameter list '()'"
---

A function declaration requires a parameter list enclosed in parentheses `()` after the function name, even when the function accepts no parameters.

## Example

This error occurs when a function body or return type immediately follows the function name without `()`:

```kura
fn greet {
  Text("Hello")
}
```

It also occurs when a return type annotation is provided without an explicit parameter list:

```kura
fn default_padding -> Float {
  8.0
}
```

## Solution

Add empty parentheses `()` after the function name:

```kura
fn greet() {
  Text("Hello")
}

fn default_padding() -> Float {
  8.0
}
```
